    "mgt2": {
      "demo": {
        "order": 22,
        "cliff": "chargen has nothing to run against without one",
        "teaches": [
          "One career Item carries the whole of a career: qualification, one rank ladder, one assignment with its survival and advancement checks, three skill tables, a benefit table, an event table and a mishap table.",
          "Every row is a {text, mode, grants[]} triple — text is what the player reads, grants[] is what the screen applies, and mode: oneOf is what makes the player choose.",
          "A tray entry on an event row is a modifier put aside for later: a DM that waits for the next qualification roll, an unlock, a prohibition.",
          "standingModifiers[] is the career's own permanent DM, gated on a characteristic and scoped to one step."
        ],
        "trap": "The eleven fields below the tables — assignment, terms, rank, ladder, enlistedRank, events, entryMode, exitMode, termLog, track — are the record half of this type, and they stay empty on a template. The same Item type is both the career a Traveller may enter and the career a Traveller served; termLog is what tells the two apart."
      }
    }
  },
